Expected elements: present

All backbone items are on the page: identity bar with truncated hash, `Partial` badge, an exit landing on the chain (`← demo`), both stepping directions, a determinate scrubber, `128 / 1315`, the phase rail; the provenance marker as the first labelled row of the Transaction pane (`DATA` + `Synthetic demo data` + the producer's own sentences); Code with line 32 highlighted; a seven-frame call trace tabbed with Event Log, Call Trace open; Values as a pane below. No provenance band, no prose band, no spinner, no empty pane. This reads unmistakably as the desktop app.

(a) landed — the EXECUTIONS note is now a capitalised sentence with a terminal stop. (b) landed — SELECTOR and RAW both render an em dash, and declining "None published" was right. (d) landed and landed *conditionally*, which is better than promised: the fade appears on the Code pane and the RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE) block, and correctly does not appear over the call trace's empty lower half.

Where machine vocabulary still surfaces: `Status reason: private-part-succeeded-public-part-succeeded` (re-filed, P2); `mana (FeeJuice)` in COST · MANA, where the label was humanised but the value was not (P2); `BLOCK 101:0`; two rows both labelled `RAW`. Separately, the Code pane's notice strip states something the render contradicts (P2).

Highest-priority fixes: rewrite the status reason as a sentence, and fix the Code pane notice — it tells a reader to look off-screen for a marker that is on-screen six rows down.

